 - **The grid's CSS:** the inventory includes `card_grid`, so the grid's CSS is
   attached on /vehicles as well.
+
+## The Location & Hours page (R03)
+
+Built in R03 (`droost/intake/tickets/R03.md`; spec
+`droost/droost-workflow/spec-r03-location.md`).
+
+- **The page:** `/location` is a Canvas page, "Location & Hours", with two
+  roots (HR2): `page_head`, then `split`.
+  - `split`'s `main` slot holds `map_card` and two `info_card`s: "Address",
+    whose `content` slot holds `dealership_address`, and "Before you head
+    over".
+  - Its `aside` slot holds `hours_table` and `closing_cta` with
+    `kind: panel`.
+- **The title:** the `canvas_page` metatag default is
+  `[canvas_page:title] — [site:name]`, so every Canvas page is titled the way
+  the source's are. The description is the page's own field.
+- **Rebuilding:** `wildbills_site_deploy_r03_location()` (`drush deploy:hook`)
+  makes the page and the `/location.html` redirect. Then
+  `droost/canvas/apply-location.sh` finds the page by its alias and writes
+  `droost/canvas/location.tree.json` with `tree:validate` and `tree:set`.
+
+### The location components
+
+All are enabled in Canvas. Their copy (headings, sentences, labels, the
+caption, the note, the status placeholder) is props. The status lines, the
+"· today" mark and the "sample" tag are interface strings in code, translatable
+(`Drupal.t`, `|t`), as the home hero's "sample" is.
+
+- **What comes from the details:** the address, the map links and the hours
+  never come from props. `LocationDetails` (in `wildbills_site`) hands them in
+  as variables Canvas does not offer.
+  - `map_card` gets `google_url` and `apple_url`.
+  - `dealership_address` gets `street` and `city`.
+  - `hours_table` gets `days` and `timezone`.
+- **`split`:** two columns (1.3fr / 1fr), one column under 900px.
+- **`map_card`:** the source's SVG art (decorative), the pin and its caption
+  (Q6: not a real map). Its two buttons open in a new tab: `button` gained
+  `new_tab` for them.
+- **`info_card`:** a heading under a rule, a `sample` switch (the tag shows
+  only while the demo notices are on), a sentence, a link and a `content`
+  slot. R04's contact cards are meant to reuse it.
+- **`closing_cta`:** `kind: section` is the home page's panel, unchanged.
+  `kind: panel` is the compact single-column card in a column.
+- **Shared type:** `.wb-tag-sample` is in `css/base.css`, since the info card
+  and the hours table both show it. Everything else is in its component's
+  CSS; the hours note is `.wb-hours-note`, so it does not touch the
+  inventory's own `.wb-note`.
+
+### The open status (Q8)
+
+- **Where it is worked out:** in the browser, by `hours_table.js`. The page
+  cache keeps a page until the details change, so a status printed by the
+  server would freeze.
+- **Which clock:** the dealership's time zone (`data-timezone`), read with
+  `Intl.DateTimeFormat`, never the visitor's.
+  - It marks today: `.is-today`, `aria-current="date"`, "· today".
+  - It writes the source's `openStatus()` lines: "Open now · closes 7:00pm",
+    "Closed · opens today at …", "… tomorrow at …", "… <day> at …".
+- **Formatting:** times are formatted once, on the server (`HoursTable`). The
+  script only compares minutes and reuses the labels.
+- **Without JavaScript:** the week still lists, and the status stays at its
+  placeholder, "Checking hours…".
